The forward lens copies an optional field (from.count, line 7 of 1.0) that the
data lacks, so its result would be incomplete. Before lens totality was proven
at bind, only Translate found it, and wrapped the evaluator's error with
fmt.Errorf so that its position (the mapping itself) survived only as text.

Bind now refuses the lens (checkLensTotality) at the mapping, as a structured
position, together with the bound the copy also narrows (count: int & <10,
line 3), which the data in this case happens not to exercise.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count?: int
}
-- ship/1.0.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count: int & <10
}

forward: {
	count: from.count
}

backward: {
	count: to.count
}
-- data.json --
{"title": "a"}
-- out/error --
lens 0.0->1.0 is not total over schema 0.0:
    ship/1.0.thema:6:1
lens 0.0->1.0: result.count copies input.count, which is now int & <10, which does not accept every value of the prior int (compat rule value-narrowed) (rule copy-narrowed):
    ship/1.0.thema:7:9
lens 0.0->1.0: result.count copies input.count, which may be absent: input.count is optional in the source schema; guard the field with if input.count != _|_ (rule source-absent):
    ship/1.0.thema:7:9
-- out/positions --
lens 0.0->1.0 is not total over schema 0.0
	authored ship/1.0.thema:6:1
lens 0.0->1.0: result.count copies input.count, which is now int & <10, which does not accept every value of the prior int (compat rule value-narrowed) (rule copy-narrowed)
	authored ship/1.0.thema:7:9
lens 0.0->1.0: result.count copies input.count, which may be absent: input.count is optional in the source schema; guard the field with if input.count != _|_ (rule source-absent)
	authored ship/1.0.thema:7:9
